{
  "original_id": "newwin-00001-p07",
  "archive_id": "BW2-N01-P07",
  "title": "A bijection for 312/321-avoiding permutations whose cubes avoid 2143",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer n>=0, let B_n be the permutations pi of [n] avoiding classical patterns 312 and 321 whose third compositional power pi^3 avoids 2143; no condition is imposed on pi^2. Let C_n be the ordered compositions of n with at most one part outside {1,3}, with one empty object in each set at n=0. Writing epsilon_d=(2,3,...,d,1), with epsilon_1=(1), the direct-sum map F(d_1,...,d_m)=epsilon_{d_1} direct-sum ... direct-sum epsilon_{d_m} restricts to a size-preserving bijection C_n -> B_n. Its inverse repeatedly records the position d of the minimum, removes the forced prefix epsilon_d, and subtracts d from the suffix. For every finite list of positive parts, F(d)^3 avoids 2143 if and only if at most one part is outside {1,3}. Consequently b_n=|B_n|=|C_n| for all n>=0 and, as a formal power-series identity, sum_{n>=0} b_n z^n = 1/(1-z-z^3) + (z^2+z^4/(1-z))/(1-z-z^3)^2.",
